ment-5611662713","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123346","id":5611662713,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABTnsteQ","user":{"login":"Acamaeda","id":19804846,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODA0ODQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19804846?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Acamaeda","html_url":"https://github.com/Acamaeda","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Acamaeda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Acamaeda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Acamaeda/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Acamaeda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Acamaeda/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Acamaeda/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Acamaeda/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Acamaeda/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Acamaeda/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-10T02:17:33Z","updated_at":"2026-09-10T02:17:33Z","body":"It's currently the only way to allow small values in certain values in the editor other than changing the setting that affects it for all values, which could cause other issues since presumably there's a reason that small values are rounded in the first place.\n\nIf hide_control is set, would there still be division errors since there's nothing actually using the step size?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5611662713/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5614016098","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123346#issuecomment-5614016098","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123346","id":5614016098,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABTp8WYg","user":{"login":"Oblepikha","id":77234360,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3MjM0MzYw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77234360?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha","html_url":"https://github.com/Oblepikha","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-10T06:11:03Z","updated_at":"2026-09-10T06:11:03Z","body":"Why do you need such a small step? Is it a molecule simulation or a large world?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5614016098/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5647054462","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123346#issuecomment-5647054462","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123346","id":5647054462,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUJc2fg","user":{"login":"Acamaeda","id":19804846,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODA0ODQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19804846?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Acamaeda","html_url":"https://github.com/Acamaeda","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Acamaeda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Acamaeda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Acamaeda/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Acamaeda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Acamaeda/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Acamaeda/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Acamaeda/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Acamaeda/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Acamaeda/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-12T16:08:58Z","updated_at":"2026-09-12T16:08:58Z","body":"I'm making a Katamari-like level editor. People can set sizes and other values for various objects, which can be very large or small, and arbitrary limitations would be confusing.\n\nIf that's too niche, at the very least the error message should be that it can't be below a certain size instead of that it can't be zero.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5647054462/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5651119642","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123346#issuecomment-5651119642","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123346","id":5651119642,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUNU-Gg","user":{"login":"Oblepikha","id":77234360,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3MjM0MzYw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77234360?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha","html_url":"https://github.com/Oblepikha","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-13T04:23:00Z","updated_at":"2026-09-13T04:32:07Z","body":"I suppose it is because `float` _has 14 reliable decimal digits of precision_.\nhttps://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_float.html#class-float\n\nAnd when you use a step of 1e-15 or less, it just gets rounded away.\nIn such an extreme case, the actual step depends heavily on the magnitude of your variable.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5651119642/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5665247528","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123346#issuecomment-5665247528","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123346","id":5665247528,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUazRKA","user":{"login":"MrAxelius","id":236461118,"node_id":"U_kgDODhgcPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/236461118?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrAxelius","html_url":"https://github.com/MrAxelius","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrAxelius/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrAxelius/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrAxelius/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrAxelius/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrAxelius/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrAxelius/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrAxelius/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrAxelius/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrAxelius/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-14T14:05:07Z","updated_at":"2026-09-14T14:07:45Z","body":"It's not an error, nor arbitrary actually. \nThis happens because floating point representation, (the way computers see numbers) has a fixed amount of bits, 32 in GDScript. This amount of bits is not enough to actually represent numbers below 1e-14. Therefore, it's not something that can be solved from software level.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5665247528/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5665686601","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123346#issuecomment-5665686601","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123346","id":5665686601,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUbOESQ","user":{"login":"Oblepikha","id":77234360,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3MjM0MzYw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77234360?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha","html_url":"https://github.com/Oblepikha","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oblepikha/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-14T14:36:01Z","updated_at":"2026-09-14T14:36:01Z","body":"Actually, `@export_range` without a fixed step is kinda neat. Maybe that's worth a proposal.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5665686601/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]